(on the algorithm) It carried over well. Q4 is what changed a result, and Q6's "what does the target already provide" is where the "use their code" options showed up. Three things didn't fit cleanly:
- it expects one record per problem, but this was one goal with two neighbours;
- Q3 assumes a single authority, but here Mastra and Alinery define what their code does and you define what counts as good;
- Q1 couldn't be confirmed live because you weren't in the loop during the run.
